# tests/backrefs/octal_class.rxt -- module `backrefs` ([M6.5.2]): the CLASS position, which this module must leave byte-identical to the base tier (S5.2). Every cell here is a MUST-NOT-CHANGE pin, run with the module ENABLED
#
# GENERATED BY tests/backrefs/gen_corpus.py, and that is a property rather
# than a convenience: every expectation below was produced by driving the cell
# through libpcre2 10.46 (via the committed ctypes binding at
# docs/design/backrefs_measurements/probes/br_oracle.py) BEFORE it was written.
# python3 `re` was driven over the SAME cells in the same pass, and a block
# carries `# pcre2-only` exactly where python diverged or could not compile the
# pattern -- DETECTED, never assumed, with the first divergence and the cell
# count recorded above the marking.
#
# THAT MARKING IS THE WHOLE REASON THE GENERATOR EXISTS. This module has the
# largest oracle divergence pcrec has met: python `re` refuses EVERY
# self-reference and EVERY forward reference at compile time, has no `\g`, no
# `\k` and no `(?J)` at all, rejects the `(?<n>...)` declaring spelling, and
# refuses `(?i)` anywhere but the pattern start -- which is exactly where the
# two cells that decide WHERE the caseless flag is read live. R32 C3 found the
# first test plan marking two files python-verifiable in the direction that
# LOSES the oracle; computing the marking removes the species.
#
# Design: docs/design/backrefs_design.md. Divergences are catalogued in
# docs/dev/upstream_issues.md.

# ====================================================================
# THE CLASS POSITION IS BASE SYNTAX and this module must not touch it
# ====================================================================

# With module `backrefs` ENABLED, every cell in this file must answer exactly what the BASE tier answered before it existed: inside a class a backreference is impossible, so `\0`..`\7` are octal and `\8` `\9` `\g` `\k` are the literal characters (FIX-3/K13, 41 measured cells). Sabotage S-BR6 makes the module's atom port claim the class position too, and these twelve cells are the only thing that sees it.
pattern ^[\1]$
features backrefs
m "\x01" 0 1
n "1"

pattern ^[\10]$
features backrefs
m "\x08" 0 1
n "\x01"
n "0"

# python DIVERGES here, measured rather than assumed: "8" @0 pcre2=('m', 0, 1) python=('ERR', 'bad escape \\8 at position 2') (2 of 2 cells)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^[\8]$
features backrefs
m "8" 0 1
n "\x08"

# python DIVERGES here, measured rather than assumed: "9" @0 pcre2=('m', 0, 1) python=('ERR', 'bad escape \\9 at position 2') (2 of 2 cells)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^[\9]$
features backrefs
m "9" 0 1
n "\t"

# python DIVERGES here, measured rather than assumed: "k" @0 pcre2=('m', 0, 1) python=('ERR', 'bad escape \\k at position 2') (1 of 1 cells)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^[\k]$
features backrefs
m "k" 0 1

# python DIVERGES here, measured rather than assumed: "g" @0 pcre2=('m', 0, 1) python=('ERR', 'bad escape \\g at position 2') (1 of 1 cells)
# pcre2-only
pattern ^[\g]$
features backrefs
m "g" 0 1

pattern ^[\377]$
features backrefs
m "\xff" 0 1

# pcre2 refuses: pcre2_compile failed at offset 6: octal value is greater than \377 in 8-bit non-UTF-8 mode
pattern ^[\400]$
features backrefs
perr

pattern ^[\0]$
features backrefs
m "\x00" 0 1

pattern ^[\1-\7]$
features backrefs
m "\x01" 0 1
m "\x07" 0 1
n "\x08"

# A group IN SCOPE does not make the class position a reference: `[\1]` is still the byte 0x01.
pattern ^(a)[\1]$
features backrefs
m "a\x01" 0 2
g 1 0 1
n "aa"
